\begin_layout Subsubsection
The R Debugger
\begin_inset CommandInset label
LatexCommand label
name "subsec:The-R-Debugger"

\end_inset

\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Bio7 contains a debugger for R scripts, functions and class methods. The debugger stops at breakpoints in the editor, shows the current line and displays the variables of the current environment.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset Float figure
placement document
alignment document
wide false
sideways false
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
\align center
\begin_inset Graphics
	filename images/chapter5/r_debugger.jpg
	lyxscale 40
	width 100text%
	keepAspectRatio

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout
\begin_inset Caption Standard

\begin_layout Plain Layout
The R debugger: the debugger stepped into the method step of a Reference class which is defined in another file (World.R); the Debug Text view and the console show the steps.
\begin_inset CommandInset label
LatexCommand label
name "fig:r-debugger"

\end_inset

\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\series bold
Breakpoints:
\series default
 a double-click on the ruler of the R editor (or of the Markdown editor) sets or removes a breakpoint. The context menu of the ruler contains 
\series bold
Toggle Breakpoint
\series default
, 
\series bold
Breakpoint Properties...
\series default
 and 
\series bold
Remove All Breakpoints
\series default
. In the properties a breakpoint can get a 
\series bold
Condition
\series default
 (R stops only if the condition is TRUE), a hit count (
\series bold
Stop at hit
\series default
) or a log message (
\series bold
Log, don't stop
\series default
: the message is printed, R doesn't stop). A breakpoint in a line where R can't stop (e.g., a line of a multi-line call) moves to the next line where R can stop; a breakpoint in a line of a statement which spans several lines stops before the statement.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\series bold
Starting the debugger:
\series default
 the action 
\series bold
Debug
\series default
 of the 
\series bold
Debug
\series default
 view (opened with the first breakpoint, perspective 
\series bold
R Debug
\series default
) saves the editor and executes the script with the breakpoints. Without breakpoints the debugger stops at the first statement. With 
\series bold
Debug Function
\series default
 in the context menu of the editor R stops at the next call of the selected function (also of a function of a package); a selected call, e.g., 
\family typewriter
f(3)
\family default
, is executed immediately.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The actions of the Debug view:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
\series bold
Debug:
\series default
 starts the debugging of the script of the editor.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
\series bold
Stop (Q):
\series default
 ends the debugging.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
\series bold
Next (n):
\series default
 executes the current line.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
\series bold
Step Into (s):
\series default
 steps into the function call of the line, also into the methods of Reference classes, R6 and S7 objects.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
\series bold
Finish (f):
\series default
 finishes the current loop or function.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
\series bold
Continue (c):
\series default
 continues to the next breakpoint.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
\series bold
Run to Cursor:
\series default
 continues to the line of the cursor.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
\series bold
(?):
\series default
 prints the commands of the R browser (n, s, f, c, Q, where, help).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The commands can also be typed into the console at the 
\family typewriter
Browse[1]>
\family default
 prompt (n, s, f, c, Q or an R expression): the editor and the variables stay in sync.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The tabs of the Debug view:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
\series bold
Variables:
\series default
 the variables of the current environment with their name, class, dimension, size and value. Changed values are highlighted. A value can be edited; a double-click opens it. The context menu contains 
\series bold
Open in Table
\series default
, 
\series bold
Open Matrix as Image
\series default
, 
\series bold
Add to Watch
\series default
 and 
\series bold
Copy
\series default
. A data frame is opened in a sheet of the Bio7 table, a numeric matrix as an image in ImageJ, a numeric vector as a plot and other objects in the 
\series bold
Debug Text
\series default
 view.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
\series bold
Watch:
\series default
 R expressions which are evaluated at each stop (
\series bold
Add
\series default
, 
\series bold
Remove
\series default
).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
\series bold
Call Stack:
\series default
 the calls of the current stop; a click on a call shows its variables and its line.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
During a debugging session the mouse over a variable in the editor shows its class, its size and a preview of the value (with 
\series bold
Open in Table
\series default
). If an error occurs R stops in the environment of the error.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\series bold
Several files:
\series default
 scripts which load other R files with 
\family typewriter
source()
\family default
 (also nested) are debugged with the breakpoints of all files: the debugger opens the editor of the file of the current line. Scripts which find their own folder (e.g., with 
\family typewriter
sys.frame(1)$ofile
\family default
) work, too.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\series bold
Live changes:
\series default
 breakpoints can be set or removed during a debugging session and R files can be changed and saved: the changed functions and classes are defined again and the changes apply at the next call (the running code keeps the old version).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\series bold
R Markdown and Quarto:
\series default
 breakpoints can be set in the R chunks of *.Rmd and *.qmd documents. The R chunks are debugged as a script (not knitted: inline R code, child documents and the cache are not used), the line numbers are the lines of the document. The 
\family typewriter
params
\family default
 of the YAML header are available.
\end_layout


