\begin_layout Subsubsection
Creating a Model
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\series bold
File > New > Bio7 Simulation Project
\series default
 (or the menu of the toolbar button for new projects) creates a project with a model in Java, Python or R. The wizard asks for the name of the project, the language, the name of the class (the model), the kind of the model (a 2D grid with states or with values in ImageJ, or 3D agents in the 3D view) and for Java an optional settings panel for the WindowBuilder and an optional parallel computation. The comment at the start of the class (the script) explains the API.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\series bold
Compile Java
\series default
 creates the model and calls 
\family typewriter
init()
\family default
: the grid opens in the ImageJ-Canvas view (the agents in the 3D view, geospatial agents on the WorldWind globe) with a 
\series bold
Settings
\series default
 view. The first setup arranges the views in the
\series bold
Custom
\series default
 perspective: the settings on the left (below the options of the display, e.g., Options3D or the options of WorldWind), on the right the editor above the display of the model and the view Charts beside the display. With
\family typewriter
 arrangeViews = false
\family default
 the views open in the current perspective.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
The 
\series bold
Play/Pause
\series default
 button of the toolbar calls 
\family typewriter
step()
\family default
 repeatedly (its menu sets the time interval), the 
\series bold
Setup
\series default
 button calls 
\family typewriter
init()
\family default
 again. The button shows the state of the simulation: a pause icon while the model runs, a play icon while it is paused.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
The 
\series bold
Settings
\series default
 view has the same controls at the top: 
\series bold
Play/Pause
\series default
, 
\series bold
Step
\series default
 (one time step while paused), 
\series bold
Setup
\series default
 (a new start, the counter at 0) and the speed (the slider of the Control view), followed by the settings of the model and 
\series bold
Export HTML...
\series default
.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
A new model (a compiled class or a script) pauses the simulation, resets the counter of the time steps and opens the Custom perspective new: the panels of the model before (settings, charts) are closed. If the model draws charts, the view 
\series bold
Charts
\series default
 is shown from the start (beside the display).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsubsection
The Classes of the API
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\family typewriter
GridModel
\family default
: a grid of cells with integer states and a palette of colors (e.g., cellular automata, a forest fire, an epidemic).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\family typewriter
ValueGridModel
\family default
: a grid of double values with a color map (e.g., a diffusion, a reaction-diffusion).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\family typewriter
AgentModel
\family default
 with 
\family typewriter
Agent
\family default
: agents in a 3D box, displayed as spheres in the 3D view (e.g., a swarm, a predator-prey model).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\family typewriter
GeoGridModel
\family default
: a georeferenced grid whose data (rasters and vectors in all formats of GDAL) is read with GDAL in 
\family typewriter
load()
\family default
 (e.g., a wildfire on a terrain with land cover data).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\family typewriter
GeoAgentModel
\family default
 with 
\family typewriter
GeoAgent
\family default
: agents on the Earth (longitude, latitude, altitude), displayed as points or OpenGL 3D shapes on the WorldWind globe (e.g., a bird migration, an epidemic in cities).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
A small model (a Game of Life):
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
public class Life extends GridModel {
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

    @Param(label = "Start density", min = 0, max = 1, step = 0.01, restart = true)
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

    double density = 0.3;
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset


\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

    public void init() {
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

        size(120, 120);
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

        palette("#ffffff", "#1f3a93");
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

        for (int i = 0; i < cells.length; i++)
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

            cells[i] = random() < density ? 1 : 0;
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

    }
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset


\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

    public void step() {
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

        for (int y = 0; y < height; y++)
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

            for (int x = 0; x < width; x++) {
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

                int n = countNeighbors(x, y, 1);
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

                setNext(x, y, get(x, y) == 1 ? (n == 2 || n == 3 ? 1 : 0) : (n == 3 ? 1 : 0));
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

            }
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

        swap();
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

        chart("Living cells", count(1));
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

    }
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

}
\end_layout

