\begin_layout Subsubsection
Models in Python and R
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The same models can be written in Python and in R. A script uses the module
\family typewriter
bio7sim
\family default
of the embedded Python (numpy arrays) or the functions of
\family typewriter
bio7sim
\family default
of the embedded R (matrices and data frames; no package is needed). The last line
\family typewriter
simulation(model)
\family default
starts the model in Bio7: a Java model of the same kind displays the state of the script (ImageJ, the 3D view, the WorldWind globe) and shows its settings and buttons in the Custom perspective. Play/Pause, Setup, the Settings view and the HTML export work as for Java models.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The Game of Life in Python:
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
from bio7sim import GridModel, param, action, simulation
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code

\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
class Life(GridModel):
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
