How to Export a GUI
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
Design the GUI with the WindowBuilder (a class which extends Composite) and save it.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
In the Project Explorer open the context menu of the Java file of the GUI and select 
\series bold
WindowBuilder Apps > Create Shiny App (WindowBuilder Shiny)
\series default
 or 
\series bold
WindowBuilder Apps > Create JavaScript App (WindowBuilder JavaScript)
\series default
.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
The first time, a dialog asks for the location of the app: 
\series bold
A new project
\series default
 (to edit and share the app on its own, the default name is 
\family typewriter
<class>_Shiny
\family default
 or 
\family typewriter
<class>_Web
\family default
), 
\series bold
A folder in the project of the GUI class
\series default
 (
\family typewriter
shiny/<class>
\family default
 or 
\family typewriter
web/<class>
\family default
) or 
\series bold
A folder of the workspace
\series default
 (
\series bold
Browse...
\series default
). Bio7 remembers the choice for this GUI class: later exports write to the same location without a question. 
\series bold
Change Shiny App Location...
\series default
 and 
\series bold
Change JavaScript App Location...
\series default
