\begin_layout Subsection*
5.1.5 The Flow Editor
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The Flow editor of the Bio7 application is capable to handle and execute
 different files by their extension and display and arrange them in a flowchart
 like structure.The Flow editor is useful to:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
It can be used to create complex sensitivity analysis for created models
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
It can serve as a guide for complex analysis of all tools offered by Bio7.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Or it simply can be used to visualize complex workflows.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The main strength of this tool is that you can assemble all methods and
 information, created by files for modeling, statistical analysis or image
 analysis in a profound analysis.
 The Flow editor of Bio7 helps to organize and visualize the creation and
 analysis of ecological models.
 A flowchart by definition is a graphic representation of a sequence of
 operations.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset Float figure
wide false
sideways false
status collapsed

\begin_layout Plain Layout
\align center
\begin_inset Graphics
	filename images/chapter5/flow.jpg
	lyxscale 40
	width 100text%
	keepAspectRatio

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout
\begin_inset Caption Standard

\begin_layout Plain Layout
The Flow editor
\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\end_inset

If the editor is opened default actions will be added to the Bio7 toolbar
\series bold
 (1)
\series default
 and a new menu will appear in the menubar of the application.
 Additionally, a specialized context menu will be available for calling
 different methods inside the Flow editor.
 In the flowchart of Bio7 files can simply be dragged from the 
\series bold
Project Explorer
\series default

\series bold
 (2)
\series default
 of Bio7 and dropped into the Flow editor 
\series bold
(3)
\series default
 of the application.
 According to their file extension these files are executed in the sequence
 of the flow which has been created.
 A created Flow editor file has the extension *.ecoflow.
 Some other files will be handled by default from the Flow editor when they
 are dragged from outside the workspace.
 Executable files (*.exe) will be executed, too and it is also possible to
 execute these files with an argument (by creating a file with the extension
 *.argument).
 Files from external that have different extensions will be executed according
 to their registration in the system environment.
 Furthermore an 
\series bold
Outline
\series default
 view
\series bold
 (4)
\series default
 on the left will show an overview of the flow - if the flow cannot easily
 be displayed in the main window because of its size a blue rectangle will
 be displayed in the 
\series bold
Outline
\series default
 for a flow selection.
 The selection is the area of the flow which can be displayed in the main
 Flow editor window.
 A new 
\series bold
Palette
\series default
 bar 
\series bold
(5)
\series default
 will also be displayed for inserting flowchart elements in a newly created
 file.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsubsection
Execute and Verify a Flow
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The execution of a flow will be triggered with the item 
\series bold
FlowAction
\series default
 in the top-right of the toolbar 
